{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290730-the-great-deliberation","id":1290730,"title":"The Great Deliberation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-22T06:10:02-08:00","id":1290730,"title":"The Great Deliberation","content":":: If you are part of an NYC group and you know an old dog named Beaux don\u2019t read this thread ::<br /> <br /> <br /> In an upcoming session, my solar players are going to have the opportunity to participate in a dialectic and legal argument that will determine Yu-Shan\u2019s reaction to a petition to cease the cycle of celestial (but not sidereal) exaltations. <br /> <br /> So my question to the community is this; \u201cwhat are some arguments that various exalt types could make in favor of or against the idea that heaven might decide to cancel or modify the cycle and governance of celestial exaltations.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24444-fizzlemeyer","name":"Fizzlemeyer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24444_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:20:12-08:00","id":1290732,"title":"","content":"Ohohohoho...<br /> <br /> The big one is going to be the Bronze vs Gold argument. The Sidereals will advance it heavily, but I can see other parties and PCs falling into it. Celestial Exaltation could be argued as the best tool to heal Creation's various ills and improve the lives of its populous. But at the same time it can be argued as a dangerous factor; the Exalted are unpredictable and their actions destablize Creation (and the domains of various Heavenly deities by proxy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:47:40-08:00","id":1290741,"title":"","content":"Would stopping Solar exaltations stop Abyssal/Infernal exaltations? Many might argue it's a small price to pay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:59:26-08:00","id":1290745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290730-the-great-deliberation?p=1290741#post1290741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would stopping Solar exaltations stop Abyssal/Infernal exaltations? Many might argue it's a small price to pay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's something interesting to be said about Abyssals and Infernals (theoretically) having greater self control than a Solar in limit break. Since their manifestation of the Great Curse is supposedly different as of 3e, this may no longer be the case, but i've always thought it interesting that Abyssals and Infernals had less of a tendency to set themselves up as infallible paladins (and therefore don't catastrophically fail to live up to said impossible standards). While Acts of Villainy and (especially) Resonance incentivize acting villainous, Infernals and Abyssals could attempt to minimize the damage because they're aware of the mechanism, while the Solars have historically had a great deal of trouble comprehending and planning for their potential for error.<br /> <br /> Though Yu-Shan probably wouldn't have any control over Abyssal/Infernal Exaltations in general. Even if the Deathlords and Yozis loose control of them, they're stated to seek out new hosts automatically once their bearer dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 02-22-2019, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:43:53-08:00","id":1290784,"title":"","content":"Two of the characters who will be weighing in on the debate : <br /> <br /> A lunar who wants to see only the solar bond dissolved as she sees it as a subversion of the lunars free will and effectively mental slavery. <br /> <br /> An abyssal who is asking for assistance and for heaven to formally acknowledge the abyssal exalts and assign them a given purpose similar to the Creation Ruling Mandate that is supposed to guide the solars. <br /> <br /> Infernal exalts are currently unknown to anyone in my games plotline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24444-fizzlemeyer","name":"Fizzlemeyer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24444_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:27:14-08:00","id":1290798,"title":"","content":"I assume, in your game, all of this stuff is possible? (Breaking the bond, stopping Celestial exaltation, etc)<br /> Because in the fluff it's a bit ambiguous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:57:54-08:00","id":1290810,"title":"","content":"For the Lunar, IIRC, the Solar-Lunar bond in 3e was a result of the Exalted's own actions shortly after the Divine Revolution. Though if this is going off of 2e's lore, they'd have to take the issue to UCS and Luna since they're the ones who put it in place.<br /> <br /> Well as for the Abyssal, if average gods are weighing in on this debate they're probably going to want them to seal off the Underworld or fix the cycle of reincarnation so that &quot;the proper order is restored&quot; (conveniently ignoring that the cycle was broken as a result of the Divine Revolution and the &quot;proper order&quot; was established by the Primordials they overthrew). Heaven doesn't like prayers going anywhere but to the gods. In the unlikely event that they do actually bestow something like an &quot;Underworld Ruling Mandate&quot;, there comes a problem that Yu-Shan has no real authority over the Underworld so it'd be a meaningless title tinged with imperialism.<br /> <br /> Now, I can see an Abyssal negotiating an armistice where Heaven recognizes the individual Deathknight's authority over certain shadowlands or as an emissary of ancestor cults or demanding that Yu-Shan root out corruption in the reincarnation process like Taru-Han's illegal soul collection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 02-22-2019, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:09:53-08:00","id":1290815,"title":"","content":"Idea for arguments:<br /> Point to any recent atrocities committed by Dragonblooded/Lunars/Solars/Sidereals/Anyone.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded inheritance promote long-thinking viewpoints and stable governance: a family is unaging and can't die by assassination or accident, so dragonblood families in control of nations will tend to focus on building infrastructure so it can be taxed a hundred years from now, and will build rules for inheritance to prevent civil war. Note that the main dragon blood not to function like this, the Scarlet Empress, did in fact leave a massive succession crisis when she died.<br /> <br /> Solars, and to a lesser extent Lunars, are necessary to obtain the most powerful effects - solars can make N/A artifacts like no one else, can do third circle sorcery, can make land out of the wyld, etc.<br /> <br /> Solars are a threat to the world, their power opens up destruction far past what other exalts can do, we need them gone.<br /> <br /> During the time when there were no solars, the world was better/worse than during other times.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact has a strategy of destroying infrastructure so the Realm can't have it, and not creating infrastructure because the Realm might take it. Any faction that wants the world to be wealthy/easily travelable will want the Lunars to not do that, and might consider ending Lunars to be a way to do this.<br /> <br /> The Lunars have modified their exaltation before. If heaven tries to end the cycle, it is likely this will make the Lunars do so again, and who knows what will happen. Alternatively, the Lunars will likely make some kind of effort to gain control of something to restart the cycle (invade Yu-Shan, take hostages, whatever). Regardless of whether either of these work, they could cause a lot of damage to everyone else. 400 Celestial Exalted with their backs to a wall is not something anyone wants in the same reality as them, or even an adjacent one. (Optionally said by a Lunar, in the tone of voice of someone selling Fire Insurance while holding a box of matches)<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is currently not doing most of his very important job. Messing with the Solar Exaltations might make him start doing his job again, or do even less of it.<br /> <br /> Solars and Lunars, by targeted the population more or less at random, tend to give power to numerous underclasses more so than the small hereditary elite dragon blooded belong to. This is good because it helps the dispossessed/bad because it creates chaos/bad because now those people will pray to solars instead of gods/good because those solars will be eager to trade their power for connections, while the already connected dragon blooded have too strong of a bargaining position for a god to get a good deal<br /> <br /> Due to the existence of the Lunar/Solar bond, it would be cruel to remove one kind of exalted but not the other. Either both need to go, or neither.<br /> <br /> Several Legal Arguments, most of which are intended to be silly<br /> Yu-Shan does not have legal right to make decisions regarding Abyssal Exaltations, which are rightfully owned by Deathlords and/or Neverborns.<br /> Yu-Shan does not have legal right to make decisions about an Exalted in Creation, due to the Creation-Ruling Mandate. They can only legally remove a solar or lunar exaltation from the cycle if the exalt dies in Yu-Shan.<br /> The Deathlords breaking Solar exaltations out of the Jade Prison was itself an illegal act of breaking and entering as well as burglary, and should be counteracted by Yu-Shan. While the creation of the Jade Prison was of questionable legality, this is irrelevant in the face of the complete lack of information pointing at who did it.<br /> Due to oaths sworn by the Unconquered Sun, ending the cycle of Solar exaltations would require the assent of Prince Laashe, so the meeting needs to be put on hold until Luna gets him for us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:27:17-08:00","id":1290845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290730-the-great-deliberation?p=1290798#post1290798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume, in your game, all of this stuff is possible? (Breaking the bond, stopping Celestial exaltation, etc)<br /> Because in the fluff it's a bit ambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the fluff it's rather impossible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:50:12-08:00","id":1290858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290730-the-great-deliberation?p=1290798#post1290798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume, in your game, all of this stuff is possible? (Breaking the bond, stopping Celestial exaltation, etc)<br /> Because in the fluff it's a bit ambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At least theoretically possible. Or even if they are actually impossible there at least is someone who is trying and arguing for it and that is what motivates them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24444-fizzlemeyer","name":"Fizzlemeyer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24444_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T00:47:47-08:00","id":1291029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fizzlemeyer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290730-the-great-deliberation#post1290730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:: If you are part of an NYC group and you know an old dog named Beaux don\u2019t read this thread ::<br /> <br /> <br /> In an upcoming session, my solar players are going to have the opportunity to participate in a dialectic and legal argument that will determine Yu-Shan\u2019s reaction to a petition to cease the cycle of celestial (but not sidereal) exaltations. <br /> <br /> So my question to the community is this; \u201cwhat are some arguments that various exalt types could make in favor of or against the idea that heaven might decide to cancel or modify the cycle and governance of celestial exaltations.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Biggest thing I can think of is if the Exalted genuinely pray to their Patrons their is a great Chance the Incarna would be pissed the lesser gods thought it was a good idea to genocide their chosen, the beings who won the Universe for them and whom the Incarnae suffered the Law of Diminishment for. Not to mention if the Gods went nasty and threw their lot in with the Sidereals the other Exaltated would quickly find common ground, and before they all can be placed between incarnations they have a good chance of taking over the Universe, or st least decimimating the living eff out of Yu-Shan and the mortal worshipers of the biggest lobbyists. This is not something the Gods want to get into without at least ambushing the Other Exalted first, and its hella hard to pull off another Calibration Feast Style Post Usurpation secondary Usurpation/Pogrom. Fool me once and all that rot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}